{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"`AssetRetriever`","anchor":"AssetRetriever"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"AssetRetriever","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" grants access to the content of an asset located at a given URL, such as a publication package, manifest, or LCP license."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Constructing an `AssetRetriever`","anchor":"Constructing-an-AssetRetriever"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can create an instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"AssetRetriever","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPClient"},{"type":"text","text":" to enable the toolkit to perform HTTP requests and support the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"https"},{"type":"text","text":" URL schemes. You can use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultHTTPClient"},{"type":"text","text":" which provides callbacks for handling authentication when needed."}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let assetRetriever = AssetRetriever(httpClient: DefaultHTTPClient())"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Retrieving an `Asset`","anchor":"Retrieving-an-Asset"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With your fresh instance of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AssetRetriever"},{"type":"text","text":", you can open an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Asset"},{"type":"text","text":" from any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AbsoluteURL"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ From a local file.","let url = FileURL(string: \"file:\/\/\/path\/to\/book.epub\")","\/\/ or from an HTTP URL.","let url = HTTPURL(string: \"https:\/\/domain\/book.epub\")","","switch await assetRetriever.retrieve(url: url) {","    case .success(let asset):","        ...","    case .failure(let error):","        \/\/ Failed to retrieve the asset.","}"]},{"type":"aside","name":"Note","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[!IMPORTANT]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Assets created with an HTTP URL are not downloaded; they will be streamed. If that is not your intention, you need to download the file first, for example using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPClient.download()"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"AssetRetriever","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" will sniff the media type of the asset, which you can store in your bookshelf database to speed up the process next time you retrieve the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Asset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This will improve performance, especially with HTTP URL schemes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let mediaType = asset.format.mediaType","","\/\/ Speed up the retrieval with a known media type.","let result = await assetRetriever.retrieve(url: url, mediaType: mediaType)"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"`PublicationOpener`","anchor":"PublicationOpener"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PublicationOpener"},{"type":"text","text":" builds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Publication"},{"type":"text","text":" object from an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Asset"},{"type":"text","text":" using:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"code":"PublicationParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to parse the asset structure and publication metadata."}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultPublicationParser"},{"type":"text","text":" handles all the formats supported by Readium out of the box."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An optional list of "},{"code":"ContentProtection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to decrypt DRM-protected publications."}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you support Readium LCP, you can get one from the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LCPService"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let publicationOpener = PublicationOpener(","    parser: DefaultPublicationParser(","        httpClient: httpClient,","        assetRetriever: assetRetriever,","        pdfFactory: DefaultPDFDocumentFactory()","    ),","    contentProtections: [","        lcpService.contentProtection(with: LCPDialogAuthentication())","    ]",")"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Opening a `Publication`","anchor":"Opening-a-Publication"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Now that you have a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PublicationOpener","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ready, you can use it to create a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Publication","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Asset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that was previously obtained using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"AssetRetriever","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"allowUserInteraction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter is useful when supporting Readium LCP. When enabled and using a "},{"code":"LCPDialogAuthentication","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", the toolkit will prompt the user if the passphrase is missing."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let result = await publicationOpener.open(","    asset: asset,","    allowUserInteraction: true,","    sender: sender",")"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Supporting additional formats or URL schemes","anchor":"Supporting-additional-formats-or-URL-schemes"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultPublicationParser"},{"type":"text","text":" accepts additional parsers. You also have the option to use your own parser list by using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CompositePublicationParser"},{"type":"text","text":" or create your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PublicationParser"},{"type":"text","text":" for a fully customized parsing resolution strategy."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"AssetRetriever","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" offers an additional constructor that provides greater extensibility options, using:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ResourceFactory"},{"text":" which handles the URL schemes through which you can access content.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArchiveOpener"},{"type":"text","text":" which determines the types of archives (ZIP, RAR, etc.) that can be opened by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AssetRetriever"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FormatSniffer"},{"text":" which identifies the file formats that ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AssetRetriever"},{"text":" can recognize.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can use either the default implementations or implement your own for each of these components using the composite pattern. The toolkit’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CompositeResourceFactory"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CompositeArchiveOpener"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CompositeFormatSniffer"},{"type":"text","text":" provide a simple resolution strategy."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Open-Publication","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"To open a publication with Readium, you need to instantiate a couple of components: an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AssetRetriever"},{"type":"text","text":" and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PublicationOpener"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Opening a publication","role":"article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Getting-Started","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Migration-Guide","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/NavigatorOverview","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Content","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Search","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/TTS","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Accessibility","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Readium-LCP"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/NavigatorOverview":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn about the architecture, configuration, and usage of the Readium Navigator."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/NavigatorOverview","type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","title":"Navigator Overview","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/navigatoroverview"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Content":{"abstract":[],"title":"Extracting the content of a publication","type":"topic","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/readium\/content","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/Readium\/Content"},"doc://Readium/documentation/Readium/Readium-LCP":{"abstract":[{"text":"You can use the Readium Swift toolkit to download and read p